sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: complete captured Caddy publication, official cfgmgmt file and pinned SSH argv.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten rules 9, 14, 22. No result printer. The official file check feeds the native end assertion.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · Node Caddy build or Gateway release handoff
  %% kind: route.caddy_converge
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>over SSH
  Note over GW: Record the Caddy intent<br/>full public configuration
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-route-caddy
  Note over SW: Read the input
  %%> Verify the captured content hash before contacting the Node.
  SW->>N: Check the connection
  %%> Official SSH verifies the admitted host keys before cfgmgmt changes the file.
  %%> Enrolled Nodes already have their pinned host keys in the worker's known_hosts.
  SW->>N: Write the Caddyfile
  %%> Official cfgmgmt file converges /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, root:caddy, mode 0640, replacing a symlink.
  SW->>N: Validate the Caddyfile
  %%> One bounded SSH argv runs caddy validate as the caddy user.
  SW->>N: Reload Caddy
  %%> One bounded SSH argv reloads the active service. A failed validation skips this step.
  SW->>N: Check the Caddyfile
  %%> The official file check verifies content, owner and mode after reload.
  Note over SW: Check the publication
  %%> Native assert requires a compliant file check. No printer or custom failure step.
  SW-->>GW: Native terminal status<br/>captured publication
  Note over GW: Record the version<br/>after the end check
  %%> The Gateway reads one native history response and records ready, published and the captured content version.
  %%> Failure keeps the captured Operation and file for a safe rerun, with no rollback.
